From 2c308797d95b139276a385f51c1e6d04d0ded64f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FuJluH <Support@fujluh.ru>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:49:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(desktop): the per-song records a run keeps are
 bounded

Each of these maps is keyed by song id and kept for the whole run, so
listening for months grew them one entry per song played, fetched or
looked up, with nothing ever dropping out.

- Fetches kept a phase row, an ask time and a landed library id for
  every song ever asked of the server. Rows now live for the last 512
  asks (everything on its way always stays), the ask times go with the
  rows that drop, and the landed ids are the last 4096;
- learned song lengths, lyric revision counts and Discord's failed
  art times trim their oldest entries the same way.

A screen reads a missing row as FetchPhase.None, which is what an old
settled song means, so nothing shown changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
